A menu of actions for an object, opened by right-clicking it.
[Appica docs](https://appica.dev/ui/components/react/context-menu)

<%= embed AppicaUI::ContextMenuPreview, :default %>

## Usage

```ruby
ContextMenu do
  ContextMenuTrigger(class: "flex h-40 w-72 items-center justify-center rounded-xl border border-dashed") { "Right-click here" }
  ContextMenuContent do
    ContextMenuItem { "Copy" }
    ContextMenuSeparator()
    ContextMenuItem { "Delete" }
  end
end
```

`ContextMenuTrigger` is the target area (a `<div>`, or your own element with a block that takes an argument). A
right-click, a long press on touch, or Shift+F10 / the context-menu key while it has focus opens the menu at the
pointer. Everything inside is [Dropdown Menu](<%= page_path(:dropdown_menu) %>)'s parts under `ContextMenu*` names -
items, checkbox and radio items, groups, link items and submenus - with the same keyboard support. Offer the same
actions from a visible button too, for discoverability.

